@page "/HowItWorks/share-identities"
@using InvestmentTaxCalculator.Components

<HowItWorksGuideLayout PageAddress="HowItWorks/share-identities">
    <ChildContent>
        <div class="section">
            <p>
                The matching rules and the Section 104 pool work per share. The app decides which trades belong to the same
                share from the ticker and the ISIN:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>By default, tickers with different names are different shares.</li>
                <li>
                    Trades with the <strong>same ISIN</strong> are the same share, even if the ticker differs. This covers
                    renames and exchange suffixes. For example "DISm" and "DIS" with the same ISIN are one share, shown as
                    "DIS".
                </li>
                <li>
                    The <strong>same ticker with a different ISIN</strong> is kept as a separate share, because tickers are
                    reused by unrelated companies after a delisting.
                </li>
                <li>
                    A trade or event without an ISIN, such as a stock split, joins the share with the same ticker as long as
                    no ISIN says otherwise.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Options and futures are matched by their exact contract name, because a broker's ISIN for an option is the
                    ISIN of the underlying share.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="section">
            <h2 class="section-title">Linking shares yourself</h2>
            <p>
                Some events change both the ticker and the ISIN, such as inserting a new holding company (a NewCo
                reorganisation), or keep the ticker but issue a new ISIN for the same company. The app cannot tell these from
                an unrelated company, so it keeps them separate. To treat them as one share, link the old and new tickers under
                "Share identities" on the <a href="corporate-actions" class="link-styled">Corporate Actions and Events</a>
                page. Links are saved with your session when you export it.
            </p>
        </div>
    </ChildContent>
    <FurtherReading>
        <li><a href="HowItWorks/takeovers-and-spin-offs" class="link-styled">Takeovers and spin-offs</a>: when shares are exchanged for another company's</li>
    </FurtherReading>
</HowItWorksGuideLayout>
